---
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { site } from '../content';
---

<Page
  title="Privacy — Labcast"
  description="How Labcast handles information shared through its waitlist."
>
  <Header />
  <main id="main" class="container document">
    <p class="eyebrow">LAST UPDATED 16 OCTOBER 2026</p>
    <h1>
      Your details.
      <br />
      Handled with care.
    </h1>
    <p>
      This notice covers the Labcast waitlist at labcast.ai. For questions or to
      leave the list, contact <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
    </p>
    <h2>What you share</h2>
    <p>
      Joining gives us your email address and permission to send occasional
      Labcast product and early-access updates. You can optionally tell us your
      role, event plans, and whether you want to discuss early access. Please
      don’t include children’s names or private participant information.
    </p>
    <h2>How we use it</h2>
    <p>
      We use your details to manage the waitlist, send relevant updates,
      understand potential uses, and respond to requests. Early-access follow-up
      is optional. Joining does not create an account, guarantee access, or book
      an event.
    </p>
    <h2>Where it goes</h2>
    <p>
      Netlify hosts this website and processes form submissions for Labcast.
      Hosting and spam protection can also process technical information such as
      IP addresses and request data. The Labcast team can review and export
      submissions to manage the list. See{' '}
      <a href="https://www.netlify.com/privacy/">Netlify’s privacy policy</a>{' '}
      for its handling of that information.
    </p>
    <h2>Browser storage and measurement</h2>
    <p>
      This site does not include advertising trackers or third-party analytics.
      When present, campaign identifiers are included with your signup. After a
      successful signup, your email and selected audience may be held in this
      tab’s session storage to fill the optional follow-up form. That handoff is
      read and removed on the follow-up page, expires for use after 15 minutes,
      and is not used for tracking.
    </p>
    <h2>Leaving the list</h2>
    <p>
      Email{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${site.email}?subject=Labcast%20waitlist%20removal`}>
        {site.email}
      </a>{' '}
      from the address you used to ask us to stop updates, correct your details,
      or delete your waitlist information. We retain details while managing the
      waitlist and related conversations, unless you ask us to remove them.
      We’ll keep only the information needed to respect a request to stop
      messages.
    </p>
    <a href="/" class="button">
      Back to Labcast <Icon name="back" />
    </a>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Page>
